# `local.settings.json.example` (copied to `local.settings.json`, git-ignored) is this worker's real local
# configuration now: `func start` loads its `Values` into the process environment automatically, the way it
# will later load Application Settings on the deployed Function App. This file is smaller and only exists for
# `npm run try` and `npm run smoke`, which run under `tsx` directly rather than under `func start` and so never
# see `local.settings.json` — copy the same values here, `KEY=value`, one per line:
#
#   SUPABASE_URL=<same value as local.settings.json>
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<same value as local.settings.json>
#
# `npm run try` on its own needs neither: it never talks to Supabase. Only `npm run smoke` (which this workspace
# does not run against a hosted project — see README.md) needs both. `.env` is git-ignored; never put a service
# role key in the Expo app's own `.env*` files, since anything prefixed `EXPO_PUBLIC_` is bundled into the app.
